  "description": "Overview Build. Innovate. Compete. Win. Rule 1 – Eligibility Open to students and working professionals residing in India. Individual participants and teams are permitted. Recommended team size: 1–4 members. Participants must provide accurate registration information. Employees, organizers and judges should not compete in categories where they have a conflict of interest. Rule 2 – Competition Tracks Participants may submit projects under any of the six official tracks: AI & Agentic AI. HR Tech & Recruitment. Enterprise SaaS. Data & Analytics. Cloud & DevOps. Cybersecurity & Digital Trust. Rule 3 – Project Requirements Every project must include: A clear problem statement. A proposed solution. Working prototype or demonstrable implementation. Technology stack. Architecture overview. GitHub repository or equivalent source-code access for evaluation. Demo video or live demonstration. Explanation of real-world business value. Rule 4 – Originality Projects must be original or appropriately licensed. Previously developed components must be disclosed. AI-generated code and third-party tools are allowed if disclosed. Plagiarism, impersonation and unauthorized code reuse are prohibited. Participants must have permission to use all datasets and APIs. Rule 5 – Submission Submissions must be made through the official portal. Late submissions may be rejected. Incomplete submissions may be disqualified. Teams must identify all members and their respective contributions.",
